-For a prime-power modulus $p^e$, an exhaustive local test consists of the following two charts. If $V$ is a unit, divide by $V^4$ and set $V=1$; test every residue $U/V$. Otherwise $U$ is a unit, so set $U=1$ and test residues $V/U$ divisible by $p$. In either chart compare the right side of~\eqref{eq:cover} with the full set of quadratic residues modulo $p^e$. Absence in both charts rules out a primitive integral solution, including all denominator choices for a rational point. The checker also performs a separate enumeration over all primitive residue pairs. All real-sign rows have three nonpositive terms with a negative value for every nonzero real pair. These finite obstructions prove the upper image sizes used in Proposition~\ref{prop:quartics}.
